  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Production of Artisanal Dutch Cheese with small-scale local farmers in Monquentiva, Colombia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The company Van Vliet V.O.F. is a Dutch cheese producer. Due to the growing middle class in Colombia and an increase in demand for specialty cheeses, the company used Technical Assistance (DGGF-TA) to assess the commercial and technical feasibility to produce and sell Dutch Artisanal Cheese (Gouda) in Colombia. The aim of the project was to improve livelihood and income for local farmers, local rural youth and women in particular by working with a cooperative of small scale local milk farmers (COLEGA) using Dutch technology and knowhow. The project resulted in the setup of a local production facility and sales mechanisms through a joint-venture, HolaAndes. It educated local employees to produce cheese and provided training to local farmers to improve milk production, processing standards and milk quality and with this increase their competitiveness and income.The project directly supported 6 jobs, of which all youth (25 years) and 4 female. Indirectly it supported 50 jobs, enabled knowledge transfer by training 8 people to produce cheese and by training 50 farmers to enhance sustainable agricultural production processes and milk quality which benefit these farmers beyond the extent of this project. Furthermore, the project has led to a boost in local tourism which supported an additional 6 indirect jobs. The project is expected to expand to other cities and work with more milk cooperations and farmers based on the experiences of this pilot.</narrative>
  </description>
